* What is Selection Sort?

Selection Sort works like this:
Select the smallest element from the unsorted part of the array
Put it at its correct position (swap it with the first unsorted element)
Repeat this for every position
This is why it is called SELECTION sort — you select the minimum every time.


Time complexity is always n^2


Selection sort in unstable algorithm

4 10 4* 2
2 10 4* 4
2 4* 10 4
2 4* 4 10

An advantage of selection sort is :-
It takes maximum O(N) swaps while the other techniques take O(N^2) swaps.

